diff --git a/src/apu/dsp/README.md b/src/apu/dsp/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6026042
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/apu/dsp/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# Standalone DSP56300 core
+
+Source: [xemu a34bb0f8c229a9aabda46ac69184285112f65841](https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu/tree/a34bb0f8c229a9aabda46ac69184285112f65841/hw/xbox/mcpx/apu/dsp),
+the revision immediately before its new DSP backend abstraction. Copyright
+and license notices remain in each file. The interpreter/wrapper is GPL-2.0-or-later;
+the DMA source is LGPL-2.0-or-later. `COPYING` and `COPYING.LIB` contain the
+upstream license texts.
+
+The standalone adaptation replaces QEMU host helpers and trace hooks with
+`dsp_compat.h` and `trace.h`. The APU includes the canonical core/DMA types
+instead of maintaining a second, incomplete copy. `dsp_init` handles allocation
+failure. Bootstrap cache clearing has the same explicit cast as the existing
+APU reset path for MSVC. Trailing whitespace in the imported code is normalized.
+
+Fractional multiplication uses a signed 64-bit product instead of four 12-bit
+partial products. Signed 24-bit operands multiplied and shifted once fit in
+64 bits, including the most-negative operand squared. The result is split
+back into the same 8/24/24-bit accumulator words. `test_dsp_multiply.py` checks
+17,000 exact Python-integer vectors and two million comparisons against the
+original limb algorithm. Its optional `--benchmark` builds an unsanitized
+Wasm executable separately from the correctness instrumentation.
+
+Program-word caches retain typed execution handlers for both parallel and
+nonparallel instructions. Instruction-only family selection happens on a
+cache miss; operands, addressing, ALU operations and retirement remain dynamic.
+P-memory writes, DMA program uploads and bootstrap clear affected cached
+handlers. `test_dsp_dispatch.py` compares every core byte except this private
+cache against the previous dispatcher in 141,664 cold/warm cases, plus
+multi-step programs, interrupt retirement and self-modifying code. These are
+equivalence checks, not a claim of complete hardware instruction conformance.
+
+DMA transfer storage is owned by each processor and freed by `dsp_destroy`.
+The original signed `-1` capacity compares as an unsigned maximum on Wasm32,
+so its first transfer skips allocation and reads a null pointer. Capacity now
+starts at zero, uses `size_t`, and grows with checked `realloc`. Interleaved
+transfer size is computed before allocation; allocation failure stops DMA and
+sets its error flag.
+
+`tests/web/test_dsp56300.c` executes uploaded 24-bit instructions against signed
+sample data, including 1,032 saturation vectors. It also checks bootstrap,
+decoded-code invalidation, frame interrupt acknowledgement, idle, scratch DMA,
+planar-to-interleaved FIFO output, and circular-buffer wrap/offset writeback.
+The Python runner compiles the actual sources for Wasm with undefined-behavior
+checks. The same C test can be built natively with address/undefined-behavior
+sanitizers or MSVC. Instruction encodings follow the
+[DSP56300 Family Manual](https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/reference-manual/DSP56300FM.pdf).
+
+The opt-in `RECOMP_APU_DSP=1` path now connects GP/EP MMIO, guest scratch/FIFO
+transfers, reset/bootstrap transitions and frame execution in `apu_gp_ep.c`.
+It reuses the APU physical-window resolver, serializes DSP reads with the frame
+thread, and releases processor storage at shutdown. Unused cycles expire when
+a processor idles instead of accumulating credit across frames.
+
+The legacy controls use centre bin 2 for commentary and the remaining bins
+for the bed. The executable path applies these gains to GP input, preserving
+the raw VP mix and the guest's effects processing. Both paths share the raw
+commentary meter and its attack/release smoothing. Gain changes affect new
+input; existing effect tails retain the guest program's decay.
+
+`tests/web/test_gp_ep.py` also executes uploaded stereo GP and EP programs
+through the production MMIO dispatcher and bridge, including scattered-page
+bootstrap, transformed GP mixbins, EP PCM output, eight-subframe scheduling,
+FIFO wrap and reset. Intentionally non-idling firmware exercises an explicit
+diagnostic execution ceiling; this is a stability limit, not a hardware clock
+model. Real-time overruns and unsupported FIFO packets are audit failures.
+
+The default continues the legacy bypass. Retail firmware now executes in the
+opt-in path, but continuity, full instruction/effects conformance, original-Xbox
+output matching and performance remain unproven. Tests of this core and bridge
+cannot establish complete retail audio fidelity.
